From a84270a93316678ae85eb2b85d6f29673857f93c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Luca Facenda <myrepo@facenda.uk>
Date: Tue, 7 Jul 2026 19:35:50 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] align: bring implementation and eval configs in line with the
 dissertation

Cross-examined against the dissertation export (Chapters 3-4 and appendices):

- simulation/viewpoint_drift: correct the action_weight docstring to the
  Chapter 3 design weights (Watch 1.0, Sample 0.2, Avoid 0.0); the code
  and tests already implemented 0.2 but the docstring claimed 0.5
- engagement + simulation/engine: the engagement mapping now receives the
  decider's action (Chapter 4: 'the resulting action is converted into an
  explicit watch-time signal'; both agent paths 're-enter the same bounded
  action space before watch-time mapping'). Previously the heuristic
  action was recomputed internally, so in LLM mode the logged action and
  its watch time could disagree. Heuristic-mode behaviour and rng
  consumption are unchanged; custom watch_time_fn callables without an
  'action' parameter keep working
- plotting/common: detect_lock_in_episodes now reports time_to_lock_in as
  the step at which the persistence window is first satisfied, matching
  analysis.compute_lock_in_metrics and the dissertation's definition of
  lock-in as sustained distance for a consecutive window; summary.csv,
  lockin_summary.csv, figures and the Compare Runs page now agree
- plotting/common + multi_run_metrics + multi_agent_metrics: use the
  Student's t multiplier (df = n_seeds - 1) for the 95% confidence
  interval claimed in the dissertation; z=1.96 understated the interval
  at the 5-seed counts the presets use
- configs/eval/E1-E6: corpus topic weights now follow the survey-derived
  Table 3.9 distribution (Light Entertainment 0.30; Hobbies & Lifestyle
  0.50 split over health/DIY/fashion; Politics & Issues 0.10;
  Random/Other 0.10 over sports/international news). The previous
  politics-dominant corpus (0.40) contradicted the documented corpus
  generation strategy. Corpus seed and all other parameters unchanged;
  run results will differ from pre-alignment runs by design
- tests: update lock-in timing expectations to the unified definition and
  add a regression test that an explicit action drives the watch-time
  mapping

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
